# Title: Potential Persistence Attempt Via Run Keys Using Reg.EXE
# ID: de587dce-915e-4218-aac4-835ca6af6f70
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2021-06-28
# Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.persistence, attack.t1547.001
# Description: Detects suspicious command line reg.exe tool adding key to RUN key in Registry
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (process_path="*\\reg.exe" AND (process_exec="*reg*" AND process_exec="* add *") AND (process_exec="*Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run*" OR process_exec="*\\Software\\WOW6432Node\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run*" OR process_exec="*\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer\\Run*"))
